  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This recording captures Mountain Goats performing at The Gargoyle in St. Louis, MO, on Monday, October 23, 2006 [1]. The setlist includes fifteen songs, beginning with \"Love Love Love\" and \"Wild Sage\" before moving into \"Baboon\" and \"Color In Your Cheeks\" [1]. The performance features \"Game Shows Touch Our Lives\" and \"There Will Be No Divorce,\" followed by a segment where Franklin Bruno enters for banter [1]. The lineup continues with \"Broom People,\" \"Dance Music,\" and \"Song for Lonely Giants\" [1]. Later tracks include \"Your Belgain Things,\" \"In The Hidden Places,\" and \"Lion's Teeth\" [1]. The set concludes with \"This Year\" and \"Houseguest\" [1]. This file is the only available recording of the event, running for 61 minutes [1]. It was taped and transferred by Matt Meshulam, who noted in the description that this was his first time recording a concert [1]. The recording is rated 4.5 out of 5 by four listeners [1]. One listener, Caliclimber, provided the missing song titles and thanked the uploader for the great sound [2]. Another listener, Gardenhead, expressed that a new Mountain Goats show always makes their day [3]. A third listener, EvilLawnGnome, commented on the use of noise reduction in the final mix, cautioning that such filters can sometimes lose detail [4]. A final listener, MovingWater, noted that John Darnielle is a compulsive talker whose banter is part of his charm, expressing a preference for the stories at the beginning of songs [5]. This is show 104 of 467 in the archive's collection for the performer [6]. The previous archived show was at the Bowery Ballroom on October 1, 2006 [6].",
